  But this is a session lifetime, so I want your explicit go-ahead before editing.

  [1mConsequence:[0m a 16x longer session window means a stolen session token or an unattended logged-in browser stays valid
  for a full workday instead of half an hour. Idle sessions on shared or lost devices remain usable, and if there's no
  separate absolute cap or re-auth step for sensitive actions, 8 hours is the full blast radius of a hijacked session.

  Worth knowing: this config has a single flat timeout, so there's no distinction between idle timeout and absolute
  session lifetime. 8 hours as an [3midle[0m timeout is far more aggressive than 8 hours as an absolute cap with a shorter
  idle window — but implementing that split would be more than a value change, so I'm not doing it unless you ask.

